---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="MBR City News"
  description="District-wide news across MBR City — what's genuinely changing across communities, not one community's own updates."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">News</p>
    <h1>What's changing, district-wide</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page covers what's changing across MBR City's communities, not
      what's hyper-local to just one of them — and it's kept separate from
      <a href="/events/">events</a>, since "what's changed" and "what's on
      this week" are different questions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What counts as district-wide here</h2>
    <p>
      New Meydan One Mall tenants, infrastructure or road changes affecting
      the district as a whole, and community developments completing new
      phases. For what's changing inside one specific community, that
      content lives on that community's own site where one exists —
      Riviera's <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/news/">own news page</a>
      is the model this network follows as it covers more of MBR City's
      individual communities the same way.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

